1. Import the necessary packages:
```go
import (
    "fmt"
    "log"
    "net/http"
)
```

2. Create a function to handle the request:
```go
func makeGetRequest(url string) error {
    // Create a new HTTP client
    c := &http.Client{}

    // Define the URL for your GET request
    url = fmt.Sprintf("https://example.com/path?param=value")

    // Make a GET request
    resp, err := c.Get(url)
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }
    defer resp.Body.Close()

    // Check if the response was successful
    if resp.StatusCode == http.StatusOK {
        log.Printf("%s", "Request successful")
        fmt.Println(resp)
    } else {
        log.Printf("Response not successful: %s, Status Code: %d",
            url, resp.StatusCode)
    }

    return nil
}
```

3. Call the `makeGetRequest` function with your desired URL:
```go
if err := makeGetRequest("https://example.com/path?param=value"); err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
```

This code will send a `GET` request to the specified URL and print out whether the request was successful or not, along with the response status. Make sure to replace `"https://example.com/path?param=value"` with your actual URL.

Remember that this is just an example, so you should adapt it according to your specific needs and handle errors appropriately in production code.

