       }
   }
   ```

Each of these methods sorts the array in place and returns it. If you don't need to return the sorted array, `Arrays.sort()` is usually sufficient for performance reasons.

Remember that while sorting can be done very efficiently with built-in functions provided by Java (like the `.sort()` method on collections), there are trade-offs with memory usage when working directly with arrays due to their immutable nature in most JVM languages.

